# Entity IDs are strings

MySQL has no UUID column type. Application IDs are CHAR/VARCHAR strings end-to-end.

```python
# ❌ BAD
@router.get("/files/{file_id}")
async def get_file(file_id: uuid.UUID) -> FileResponse: ...

class FileResponse(Schema):
    file_id: uuid.UUID
```

```python
# ✅ GOOD
@router.get("/files/{file_id}")
async def get_file(file_id: str) -> FileResponse: ...

class FileResponse(Schema):
    file_id: str
```

- Path, query, body, dependency, service, and repository IDs: `str`, not `uuid.UUID`.
- Do not add a `{file_id:uuid}` converter.
- Persist and compare `row.id` as stored. Do not wrap with `uuid.UUID(row.id)`.
- Generate IDs with `str(uuid.uuid7())`.
- Provider subjects stay their protocol type. Never treat them as application IDs.
